## Repo layout (scaffold)

- `docs/plan.md` — the research report + phased plan (architecture, CUDA→ROCm map, prior art, gfx1201 findings, effort).
- `docs/limitations.md` — what works / in flight / not supported / caveats.
- `docs/quickstart.md` — the verified build + smoke path on a gfx1201 box.
- `docs/notes/PLAN.md` — living plan (phases, current state, open questions).
- `docs/notes/` — the root-cluster reports + notes (moved from the repo root, 0.3.0 alpha prep): `REPORT.md`, `WALL-NOTE.md`, the `REPORT-*.md` and `NOTES-*.md` files, `size-ratchet.json`.
- `vendor.json` — the pinned vendor fork + ref (primary/fallback) and the build flags. The pin is advisory: `scripts/build-wheel.sh` verifies the sha at build time and fails loud (the pin must resolve in the fork; re-pin in a PR when the base moves).
- `scripts/build-wheel.sh` — build the `mlx` wheel with `-DMLX_BUILD_ROCM=ON` for gfx1201 (guest-a-only: requires a ROCm gfx1201 box).
- `scripts/smoke.py` — Phase 0 smoke: is_available, matmul/softmax numerics, 0.6B generate.
- `scripts/smoke-serve.sh` — Phase 1 smoke: qmlx-serve with a 9B-class dense Qwen3.
- `scripts/size_ratchet.py` + `docs/notes/size-ratchet.json` — deterministic size gate (CI).
- `tests/` — hermetic tests (CI) + `@pytest.mark.gpu` tests (guest-a only).

## Release

Release publishing is tag-driven (`.github/workflows/release.yml`): a `v*` tag push runs `uv build` (sdist + wheel), then a guard that refuses to publish when the `pyproject.toml` version does not equal the tag (leading `v` stripped), then `uvx twine upload --non-interactive --skip-existing dist/*` to PyPI using the repo's PyPI secret (`TWINE_PASSWORD` = `secrets.PYPI_API_TOKEN`, `TWINE_USERNAME` = `__token__`). Tag pushes are the owner's action — workers never tag or publish. The 0.3.0 cut (released) published to PyPI on 2026-11-20 via this path.

## Benchmark (0.3.0-alpha)

9B work model, Q4_K mmq, gfx1201. Reference = the llama.cpp Q4_K_M 4K-box line (same box). Provenance, verbatim: "the Q4_K_M 4K-box line is the llama.cpp reference (3683.1 / 85.16 / 96.62% / 100.98% / 130.4% / 111.01 t/s); the llama.cpp Q4_K_M 4K-box line = 85.16 t/s decode (MTP K=3), 3683.1 t/s prefill (the fixed record protocol); 3558.63 = sustained (continuous duty, 96.62% of reference)" — see `docs/notes/REPORT-RELEASE020-20261112.md`, `docs/w1/`, and `docs/notes/WALL-NOTE.md`.

- **Prefill @4K, fixed record protocol:** `3683.1` (llama.cpp) vs `3719.25` (mlx-rocm) → **100.98% of reference**. ![prefill-4k](docs/diagrams/prefill-4k.svg)
- **Prefill @4K, sustained (continuous duty):** `3683.1` (llama.cpp) vs `3558.63` (mlx-rocm) → **96.62% of reference**. *Box-state caveat (declared box state, not a software defect): the sustained-continuous-duty box sits ~3% below the fixed-protocol headline line on duty-dependent shader-clock boost — see `docs/notes/WALL-NOTE.md` 2026-11-19.* ![prefill-4k-sustained](docs/diagrams/prefill-4k-sustained.svg)
- **Decode @4K ctx, MTP K=3:** `85.16` (llama.cpp) vs `111.01` (mlx-rocm, the `MTP=3` + `MTP6_PREFILL_FILL=1` env class; banked on main) → **130.4% of reference**. ![decode-4k-mtp3](docs/diagrams/decode-4k-mtp3.svg)

